WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.302
-I think for people our age,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.637
your memory of this impeachment
saga is far different.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.006
Like, you think about it,
or I think about it

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.175
when I reflect back on it,
as a political event.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.844
And this show does
a very nice job

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:14.914
of showing how
human beings were affected,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.083
and in particular, how young
Monica Lewinsky was

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.417
when this was all happening.
-Monica Lewinsky --

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.753
I mean, there are so many things
about Monica's experience

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.254
during this time
that I had no idea about.

00:00:22.254 --> 00:00:25.591
And I, too, had my own opinions
about Monica.

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:28.728
But, you know, she was held
in a hotel room by the FBI

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.397
for 12 hours while waiting
for her mother to come

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.400
from New York City to D.C.,
and, you know, it just --

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.069
When you really, really
think about it,

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:37.737
she was essentially a child.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.574
And there was one person who
should have been responsible

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.076
to not only his family,
but to the country,

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.912
and that didn't happen so much.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:46.913
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.247
-You know who I'm talking about.

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:49.748
-I do know who.
-Okay. Cool, cool.

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:52.085
I'm sort of a political junkie.
-Are you? Oh, yeah.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.752
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:56.255
-But I want to also --
you talk about responsibility.

00:00:56.255 --> 00:01:00.927
And you also, not just as an
actor but as a producer on this,

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.461
you guys obviously understood

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:03.796
you had a responsibility
as well.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.632
And I know Monica worked on it.
-She did.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.466
-But, you know, there were
other people involved.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:09.802
And, you know, Linda Tripp
is someone that I think

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.972
we all just have this one idea
of who she is.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.141
-Yeah. Detestable traitor.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.976
Betrayer of a friend. Yeah.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:20.446
-And you wanted to make sure
you got this right.

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:23.116
No to sort of sugar-coat
her behavior,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.618
but just to try to present
a more three-dimensional person.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:28.454
-Yeah, because I feel like,
why do it otherwise?

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.456
John Goodman already did
an excellent job

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.458
on "Saturday Night Live."
-Very three-dimensional.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:35.127
-Very three-dimensional,
showed all the aspects of it.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.797
I really didn't know
where to go from there.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.800
It felt like a complete thing.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.468
So, I just...

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.270
The thing is,
Linda was a wonderful mother

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.273
and subsequently
a wonderful grandmother

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.443
and had a lot of attributes
as a human being

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:54.614
that were worthwhile in terms of
the human experience.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.783
But she did do, I think,
an unforgivable,

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:01.454
very, to this day, to me,
still mysterious thing.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.457
I've tried to come up with the
reasons why I think it happened.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.459
I -- I have the reason.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.461
I let the rest of the world
determine

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.797
whether or not they think
that suffices.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.132
But, you know, I was terribly
sad when she died.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.467
-She passed away last year.
-She died in April 2020.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:16.969
We were supposed to start
shooting in March,

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:18.471
and then of course,
because of the pandemic,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.507
we didn't start shooting
till October of 2020,

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:22.841
instead of March.

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:24.844
And, you know, I got so many
texts the day she died,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:28.013
as if it were me or somebody
that I actually knew.

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:30.516
-Was she aware that you guys
were embarking on it?

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.184
-I have no idea.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:34.687
I had a fantasy of being able
to meet her one day

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.690
and just tell her
that I had a lot of --

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.358
I wouldn't say sympathy,
but empathy

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:41.527
for what she went through.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.697
-Well, I think, yeah,
what you said really rings true,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.532
and I think it's a thing
that people talk about now,

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.033
which is you can do
a terrible thing,

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.370
but there are the sort of
multitudes of every human being.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.039
-Correct.
And, you know, I do believe

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.841
deep down she thought
she was doing something

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.343
for a greater good.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:01.380
It's just probably greatly
blinded by other factors,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.049
and didn't think about
the consequences on this,

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:08.053
as we were saying,
terribly, terribly young woman.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:11.490
-You did hear -- you got
feedback from I think it was --

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.659
we were talking backstage --
one of her daughters.

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.094
-Yeah, Allison,

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.931
who is featured in the show
quite heavily as we go along.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.431
There does come a point
in the story

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:21.100
where Monica and Linda are
no longer together,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.535
where they basically
never saw each other again,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.537
so that happens.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:27.706
I was very moved by what I read
that her daughter said.

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:31.043
And for me,
as far as critics go,

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:32.745
it's the only thing
that mattered to me

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:35.581
that she in fact -- at least as
far as seeing the first episode.

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.082
She made it very clear
where she was like,

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:38.751
"I've only seen one

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:41.587
and I may not hold on to this
thought by the end of it,"

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.089
which is totally fair.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.757
But it meant that maybe,
you know --

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.792
she sort of said she wished
her mother could have seen it,

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:49.128
and that to me is...

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.830
single tear.
-Yeah, single tear.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:55.501
You mentioned your getting
your lightning bolt --

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.503
electrified hair.
-Yes.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.505
-And then you've been out
with it, right?

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.673
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.575
Yeah, that's Hypodermic Sally,

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.444
and it's not even the most
effective photograph.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:07.579
-This one kind of looks fine.
-This one looks fine.

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.581
-But there is one --
-If you were like --

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:10.950
You guys know Hypodermic Sally.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.285
You're like,
"Yeah, she's pretty hot."

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.453
Well, I want you
to meet her friend.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:15.955
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.223
-I mean, really.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.225
It's almost as if Ryan doesn't
like me very much.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.060
Isn't this what it seems like?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.396
-So, you have, you've been out
in, like, public.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.799
-I would shoot until, you know,
11:00 at night

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.300
and forget that
I looked like this,

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.503
'cause I was also shooting
Marcia Clark at the same time,

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.506
which was another really stellar
physical -- a lot of wigs.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.507
But this was my own hair.
This is not a wig, Seth.

00:04:35.507 --> 00:04:37.843
-This is the real thing?
-This is my hair.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:43.015
I would walk at night
to the supermarket, as you do,

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:45.585
and I would get my items and
I would go to pay for them,

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.653
and the gentleman behind
the counter was always like,

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:49.288
"I'll -- I'll take your..."

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.257
Like, here's a quarter and
a nickel and he's like,

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.925
"Oh, just take it.
Just take it."

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.527
'Cause it was not...

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.196
I had scratches painted on me.
It was bad.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.198
-How many times -- do you know
off the top of your head

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.367
how many times
you've worked with Ryan?

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.202
-Do I count each iteration
of "American Horror Story"?

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.537
-You do.
-Individually?

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.805
-Yeah.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.306
-So, that's nine seasons of
"American Horror Story,"

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:08.907
two seasons of "Crime Story.

00:05:08.907 --> 00:05:10.476
I did a pilot for him
called "Nip/Tuck."

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.978
I did...

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:14.313
What else did I do?

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.648
Oh, I did "Ratched."
-Yeah.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.483
-"Pretty/Handsome"
was the pilot I did.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.818
"Nip/Tuck" I did an episode of.
So, that's...

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:21.420
-Yeah, that's --
-"Feud," I was in.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.821
Did anybody count?
Was anybody counting?

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:24.657
-I think it's like 14 or 15,
but I think it's impressive.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.058
-Were you really counting?
-I was, like...

00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:27.727
I mean, there was like nine...
-You stopped at one point.

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:30.329
-You said nine, and then I was
just like, I'm just gonna add...

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:31.663
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.663 --> 00:05:32.998
-"You were like, "Night-night."

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:34.333
"Let me know when you're done
counting, Paulson."

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.468
-But it's a very
impressive number.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:39.438
You guys must have a very nice
shorthand now, I would imagine.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:40.773
-We do.
It goes like this.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.442
"Hi. This is what you're doing."
"Great. Bye."

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:45.277
-And that's sort of it.
-Now off to the wigs!

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:48.781
-Off to the wigs, and I'll see
you later, and you know.

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:51.117
-It's always great to see you.
-Really good to see you, too.

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.119
-Congratulations on the show.
Thanks for being here in person.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.453
-Thanks, man.
Thanks for having me.

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:55.788
-Next time I'll have
an audience for you.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.256
-Please do.
-I will.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.591
"Impeachment" airs Tuesdays
at 10 p.m. on FX.

00:05:59.591 --> 00:06:01.426
"American Horror Story:
Double Feature"

00:06:01.426 --> 00:06:04.263
airs Wednesdays
at 10 p.m. on FX.

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.231
and streaming the next day
via FX and Hulu --

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:07.867
You're everywhere, Sarah.
-I'm everywhere.

